"devex-faq":{"digest":"18558b8d21d4f7bc3364106cb47cbfbb46b753288dd5ea6035a6bff92ab0cefe","initialized":"2026-10-18","seen":[],"text":"An overview of what the DevEx program is, how to submit a DevEx request, and the requirements for a user to submit a request.\n\nDevEx Program Overview\n\nThe Roblox Developer Exchange Program (also known as DevEx) is a program that allows Roblox creators to exchange their Earned Robux for real money. While any creator can use Roblox Studio to learn to code, create experiences or items to enjoy with their friends, and even earn some Robux, only successful creators will be able to meet the high requirements (described below) to earn money through DevEx. Reaching this level of success typically requires a lot of time, effort, skill, and strategy. Even then, there is no guarantee of earning money. Regardless of goals, be it fun or career advancement, we offer creators what they need to start building for free at create.roblox.com.\n\nDevEx Program Application Process for New Participants\n\nHow the DevEx Process Works\n\nOnce you meet the eligibility requirements, you can join the DevEx program simply by submitting a DevEx request in the Creator Hub . Submitting a DevEx request starts a review by the DevEx team where we review your eligibility for a DevEx Payout. If approved, an invitation to the DevEx Portal is submitted where you can provide your tax and payment information. Once registration is complete, a payment can be submitted. For more information, read on below:\n\nDevEx Eligibility Requirements\n\nTo use DevEx, you must agree to the Developer Exchange Terms of Use and meet the requirements set out in those Terms, some of which are as follows:\n\nMinimum of 30,000 earned Robux in your account\n\nHave a verified email address\n\nValid DevEx portal account ( an invitation is sent after review of your first submitted DevEx request)\n\n13 years of age or older\n\nCommunity member in good standing, having complied with Roblox's Terms of Use\n\nFor the full list of DevEx eligibility requirements, please visit our Terms of Use .\n\nWhen submitting a DevEx request, please only use your legal name . Nicknames, family members, friends, or joke names may result in your account’s ineligibility to participate in the DevEx program, or significantly delay your review.\n\n________\n\nResources\n\nFor more information on the Roblox Developer Exchange program, visit the Creator Hub .","title":"Developer Exchange (DevEx) Overview, How to Submit, Requirements"},
